RECORD 15 — the three-arm ablation, PRE-REGISTERED BEFORE ANY ARM RUNS
written 2026-09-05. No ablation inference has been performed.
=============================================================================

QUESTION. Does the analyst agent improve forecast quality, and if so does its
LENGTH matter? Two arms would confound "reasoning helps" with "reasoning at length
helps", so there are three.

  ARM A  the frozen system, analyst unchanged
  ARM B  analyst capped near 1,000 max_tokens (18% of its 5,585-token mean)
  ARM C  no analyst; the structuralist reads intake's output directly

SAMPLE. Pooled development halves of both bands: clean 175 + ambiguous 174 = 349
scoreable items over 42 occupied 10-day blocks. Pooled because the estimand is a
PAIRED difference between arms on the same items, so band membership cancels; the
leakage estimate found none measurable (-0.00169 [-0.00934, +0.00603]); and 42
clusters is the binding constraint on power. The two bands are ALSO reported
separately as a pre-registered split, so the pooling objection becomes a
measurement rather than an assumption.

COST, verified before committing. Arm A is a pure cache replay -- confirmed on AAPL
2026-01-29: three cache hits of three, forecast byte-identical to the stored one
ignoring run_id. Corpus-wide, 741 of 746 intake keys reconstruct to cached files.
The analyst is 86.7% of all generated tokens, so removing or capping it is what
makes this an overnight run rather than a fortnight.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE DRAW-NOISE CONFOUND, AND ITS ESTIMATOR -- SPECIFIED IN FULL
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE PROBLEM. The analyst runs at temperature 0.7 with seed 20260809 requested, and
this backend honours seeds only partially -- measured previously at 2 of 5 replays
byte-identical. Arm A is a CACHED draw; arm B is a FRESH one. So

    A - B  =  the cap effect  +  the difference between two independent draws

and attributing the whole of it to the cap is the error this control exists to
prevent.

THE CONTROL. Fresh UNCAPPED analyst draws on 60 items -- same prompt, same
sampling, same everything as arm A, the only difference being that the call is
made rather than replayed. The 60 are chosen by the CORPUS'S OWN EXECUTION SEED
(numpy default_rng(20260830).permutation, first 60 of the shuffled 355 loaded
items), not by hand. They occupy 23 blocks, sizes min 1, median 2, max 8, mean 2.61.

THE ESTIMATOR, written out because a threshold without one is not a
pre-registration -- the defect that cost the Phase 3 success condition:

  1. For each of the 60 subsample items, the paired per-item difference
         d_i = CRPS(cached draw)  -  CRPS(fresh uncapped draw)
     scored identically to every other arm: vintage 2026-09-05 pinned, realised
     bar pinned, same baselines.

  2. Decompose d into cluster components by 10-day block, one-way random effects:
         sigma_b^2  between-block variance of the block means
         sigma_w^2  within-block variance of items about their block mean
     sigma_draw is reported as the per-item SD, sqrt(sigma_b^2 + sigma_w^2), and
     both components are reported separately.

  3. The implied cluster-robust standard error of a MEAN paired difference at the
     full comparison size is then computed DIRECTLY, not by rescaling:

         SE_349 = sqrt( ( sigma_b^2 + sigma_w^2 / n_bar ) / G )
         with G = 42 blocks and n_bar = 349/42 = 8.31 items per block.

  4. THE GATE:  |A - B|  >  2 x SE_349.
     If it fails, THE CAP EFFECT IS NOT ESTABLISHED whatever the A-B interval says,
     because that interval would be measuring draw noise with a cap-shaped label.

WHY THE SCALING IS WRITTEN AS A FORMULA AND NOT A FACTOR. The obvious shortcut is
to scale the subsample's standard error by sqrt(349/60) = 2.41. That is the
NO-CLUSTERING limit and it is wrong here. Scaling by clusters instead gives
sqrt(23/42) = 0.74. The two differ by a factor of 3.3, and the correct ratio lies
between them, determined by the measured decomposition:

    all variance within-block  (sigma_b = 0)  ->  ratio 0.41  (= 1/2.41)
    all variance between-block (sigma_w = 0)  ->  ratio 0.74

Using 2.41 would make SE_349 roughly 1.8x too small and the gate correspondingly
too easy to pass. Using 0.74 blindly would make it too strict if the noise is
mostly within-block. The formula in step 3 needs no ratio at all, which is why it
is the specification. sigma_draw, sigma_b, sigma_w and SE_349 are ALL REPORTED
whatever they are.

ARM C DOES NOT HAVE THIS PROBLEM, and the reason is structural: removing the
analyst removes the only stochastic component. Intake and structuralist both run at
temperature 0. So A-C is confounded by the prompt change but NOT by draw noise, and
is the cleaner architecture comparison; A-B is the cleaner length comparison but
only if the gate above clears; B-C carries both confounds.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE PROMPT CONFOUND, STATED UP FRONT
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Arm C needs a different structuralist prompt, so it changes the architecture AND
the prompt together. Any arm-C difference is attributable to either. The change is
minimal -- the input-block header and the sentence naming what is being read;
nothing about the schema, the ordering invariant, the scenario definitions or the
output contract -- and the diff is recorded VERBATIM in the ADR so a reader can
judge the size of the confound rather than take my word for it.

Arm B has a weaker form of the same problem: a capped analyst produces truncated
reasoning, which is a different input distribution and not merely a shorter one.

NONE OF THE THREE ARMS IS THE FROZEN SYSTEM EXCEPT A. B and C are new
configurations, their forecasts are NOT corpus artifacts, they are written outside
runs/, and they are never scored against the holdout, which is spent.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRICE IDENTITY -- a property, not a hope
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
All arms score against vintage 2026-09-05, pinned and READ-ONLY; a missing window
refuses rather than fetching. All 355 loaded items carry a realised-bar pin, and
the last scoring produced zero RealisedDriftError. The pin is keyed on
