RECORD 17 — the FOUR-arm ablation: arm D, what cannot be isolated, and the
comparison hierarchy. Registered before any arm runs.
=============================================================================

Supersedes record 15's three-arm design and incorporates record 16's correction.

  ARM A  frozen system            intake -> analyst 12B t=0.7 -> structuralist 4B t=0
  ARM B  capped analyst           as A, analyst max_tokens 1000 (18% of its 5,585 mean)
  ARM C  no analyst, small model  intake -> structuralist 4B t=0 on the no-analyst prompt
  ARM D  no analyst, large model  intake -> structuralist 12B t=0 on the no-analyst prompt

Arm D exists because record 16 established that A-C moves three things at once:
the analyst, the model doing the forecasting, and the prompt. D holds the model at
12B so that D-C isolates model size with the prompt held constant, and A-D isolates
the analyst with the model held constant.

IMPLEMENTATION NOTE. Arms C and D run the ordinary pipeline with a PASS-THROUGH
analyst: an object satisfying the analyst's interface that wraps intake's facts as
the narrative and makes no model call. Nothing in `execute` changes, so artifact
writing, the truncation refusal and forecast assembly are identical across all four
arms. The no-analyst prompt reuses the existing `{{narrative}}` slot, so no request
model changes either: 11 changed lines of 25.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT FOUR ARMS STILL CANNOT ISOLATE
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**No comparison in this design moves exactly one thing, and that is a property of
the architecture rather than a gap in the experiment.**

Removing the analyst forces a prompt change, because the frozen structuralist's
instructions refer to something that is no longer present -- its rule 1 is "copy
the ESTIMATE numbers from the narrative", and without an analyst there are no
ESTIMATE lines and nothing to copy. So:

  D - C   CLEAN. Model size, prompt and pipeline held constant. The only clean
          comparison in the design.
  A - D   the analyst, with the forecasting model held at 12B -- but the prompt
          differs, necessarily.
  A - B   the token budget, prompt and model held constant, but confounded by
          DRAW NOISE because A is a cached temperature-0.7 draw and B is a fresh
          one. Gated on sigma_draw below.
  A - C   three things at once. Descriptive only.
  B - C, B - D   the same, plus the cap. Descriptive only.

**THE ANALYST'S CONTRIBUTION IS NOT CLEANLY IDENTIFIABLE BY ABLATION IN THIS
ARCHITECTURE.** A-D is the closest available and still carries the prompt change.
Stating it now, before any number exists, so that a small A-D difference is not
later read as a clean measurement of what the analyst adds. The only way to remove
the confound entirely would be an architecture whose structuralist prompt does not
name its upstream -- which is a redesign, not an experiment.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMPARISON HIERARCHY AND MULTIPLICITY, FIXED NOW
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Four arms give six pairwise tests on a design whose stated prior is that nothing
differs. Testing six and reporting the smallest interval would manufacture a result.

  PRIMARY, family of two, family-wise error controlled by Bonferroni:
      A - D   the analyst, model held constant
      D - C   model size, prompt held constant
    Each is judged at a BONFERRONI-CORRECTED 97.5% cluster-robust interval --
    bootstrap percentiles 1.25 and 98.75 rather than 2.5 and 97.5. A primary that
    excludes zero at 95% but not at 97.5% IS REPORTED AS NOT ESTABLISHED.

  SECONDARY, one test, reported at an uncorrected 95% interval and explicitly NOT
  part of the family:
      A - B   the token budget, additionally gated on sigma_draw

  REPORTED BUT NOT TESTED: A-C, B-C, B-D. Point estimates and intervals are shown
  for completeness; NO INFERENTIAL CLAIM is made from them and they carry no
  correction because none is being claimed.

The primary pair was chosen for being the two least confounded comparisons
available, before seeing any number. It is not revisable after.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SIGMA_DRAW -- unchanged from record 15, restated because the gate is load-bearing
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
60-item subsample, chosen by the corpus execution seed, 23 blocks.
  d_i = CRPS(cached draw) - CRPS(fresh uncapped draw), per item
  decompose by 10-day block: sigma_b^2 between, sigma_w^2 within
  SE_349 = sqrt( ( sigma_b^2 + sigma_w^2 / 8.31 ) / 42 )
  GATE: |A - B| > 2 x SE_349, else the cap effect is NOT ESTABLISHED
sigma_b, sigma_w, sigma_draw and SE_349 are all reported whatever they are.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
PREDICTIONS AND POWER
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRIOR, unchanged: THE ARMS WILL BE HARD TO TELL APART. P(up) spans 0.369-0.631 and
the volatility slope is near 0.4; most of what reaches the forecast is the document
and the trailing volatility, both of which survive removing the analyst.

  ALL FOUR INDISTINGUISHABLE  ->  no component measurably improves CRPS on this
    corpus, and the 12B analyst -- 86.7% of all generated tokens -- is the most
    expensive part with no demonstrated benefit. The most likely outcome.
  A BETTER THAN D  ->  the analyst contributes beyond its model size. The
    architecture's hypothesis gets its first support, with the prompt caveat.
  D BETTER THAN C  ->  model size matters more than the pipeline stage. The clean
    comparison, and the one whose result is least arguable.
  D BETTER THAN A  ->  the analyst actively harms at fixed model size. Reported
    prominently and not explained away.
  P(up) SPAN WIDENS WITHOUT THE ANALYST  ->  the three-scenario frame compresses
    the directional claim (Findings #46). Independent of the CRPS result.

POWER: at 349 items over 42 blocks, expect a CRPS interval half-width near 0.0008
against a mean near 0.032 at 95%; the Bonferroni primaries are wider still. THE
DESIGN CAN DETECT ROUGHLY A 2.5-3% DIFFERENCE AND CANNOT DETECT 1%. A null is
reported as "no difference larger than about 3%", never as "no difference".

