-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARM D — a BUG FIX, not a design change
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Record 17 registered arm D as "the 12B on arm C's no-analyst prompt". The
implementation handed it `registry.spec("structuralist").sampling`, whose
`max_tokens` is None, because the 4B structuralist answers directly and needs no
bound. Unbounded, the 12B reasoned for 15,406 tokens and produced no answer.

`max_tokens` is set to 12,000, matching the analyst's registered budget. **None was
never the design** -- record 17 says "the 12B on arm C's prompt", and the 12B's
budget in every frozen configuration is 12,000. This is a defect in my wiring,
corrected to what was registered, and it changes no parameter the design specified.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARM B — DROPPED, and here is why before any primary number exists
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. THE REGISTERED PREMISE IS FALSIFIED. Record 17 describes the cap as "analyst
   max_tokens 1000 (18% of its 5,585 mean)", treating it as a LENGTH manipulation.
   It is not one. gemma-4-12b-qat is a reasoning model: at a 1,000 cap it emitted
   997 reasoning tokens and no answer at all. The cap removes the ANSWER, not the
   reasoning. The arm does not measure a shorter analyst; it measures a broken one.

2. ANY REPAIRED CAP CREATES DIFFERENTIAL ATTRITION. Raise the cap and the items
   that still fail are exactly those whose documents need more reasoning. The
   completed set is then biased toward easier documents, and comparing it against
   arm A -- which has every item -- makes the estimand near-circular: the capped
   arm looks good partly because the hard items dropped out.

3. THE CAP VALUE WOULD BE FITTED TO A FAILURE. Choosing 3,000 or 4,000 means
   choosing a design parameter empirically after watching 1,000 fail. That is the
   thing this project's pre-registration discipline exists to prevent, and it is
   not made acceptable by the parameter being about cost rather than about a
   result.

4. NOTHING ABOUT AN OUTCOME IS BEING AVOIDED. Arm B produced no forecast, no CRPS
   and no comparison. There is no inconvenient result to escape, and this record is
   written before the two primaries have produced one either.

THE SIGMA_DRAW CONTROL GOES WITH IT. The 60-item control existed for exactly one
purpose: to gate A-B against draw noise, because A is a cached temperature-0.7 draw
and B was a fresh one. With A-B gone there is no comparison it gates. Arms C and D
run the structuralist at temperature 0 with a pass-through analyst, so neither
carries the analyst's stochasticity, and A-D compares a cached draw against a
DETERMINISTIC arm -- draw noise enters A only, as a fixed property of the arm
rather than as a difference between two draws. The control is not run. Its
specification stands in record 15 and 17 for anyone who later needs it.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE FAILURE IS A FINDING, and a better one than the comparison would have been
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**THIS PIPELINE CANNOT BE MADE CHEAPER BY CAPPING THE ANALYST.** The analyst is
86.7% of all generated tokens and the obvious economy is to let it think less. It
does not work, and the reason generalises beyond this project: on a reasoning model
the token budget is spent on reasoning FIRST and the answer LAST, so a budget cut
truncates the output rather than the deliberation. At 1,000 tokens, 99.7% went to
reasoning and nothing came back.

The practical consequence is that the cost of a reasoning agent is not tunable by
its budget. It is tunable only by removing the agent (arms C and D), by choosing a
model that reasons less, or by a provider-side control over reasoning effort that
this backend does not expose. That is worth more than the A-B comparison would have
been, and it was obtained for the price of two smoke-test items.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE LENGTH QUESTION, SALVAGED OBSERVATIONALLY -- NOT A SUBSTITUTE
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
The 719 completed analyst calls already carry their own completion-token counts, so
the association between reasoning length and forecast quality can be LOOKED AT
without running anything: regress per-item CRPS on analyst completion tokens across
the existing corpus.

**IT IS CONFOUNDED BY DOCUMENT DIFFICULTY AND IS NOT THE EXPERIMENT.** A harder
filing plausibly causes both longer reasoning and a worse forecast, which would
produce a positive slope with no causal content whatsoever. It has no random
assignment, no attrition control and no counterfactual. It is reported as
DESCRIPTIVE, labelled as such wherever it appears, and it must never be written up
as evidence about what capping the analyst would do. Its one virtue is that it is
free and has no attrition, which is precisely what the repaired arm B could not
offer.

PRIMARIES A-D AND D-C ARE UNAFFECTED, along with their Bonferroni-corrected 97.5%
intervals and the hierarchy of record 17. A-C, B-C and B-D as descriptive
comparisons lose their B members; A-C remains.

