RECORD 20 — the control is RE-PURPOSED: re-derivation variance, descriptive only.
Written 2026-09-05 before the control runs. Arm A complete, arm C mid-run, no
comparison computed for any arm.
=============================================================================

The 60-item control was registered in records 15 and 17 to estimate sigma_draw and
GATE the A-B comparison. Record 19 dropped arm B, so the gate has nothing to gate.
The control is kept and its purpose is restated here BEFORE it runs.

NEW PURPOSE: measure RE-DERIVATION VARIANCE -- how much a cold re-run moves the
score. Nothing else in this project measures it.

WHY IT IS WORTH KEEPING. The README supports "re-derivable does not hold" with a
BYTE-IDENTITY statistic: replaying five identical recorded prompts returned
byte-identical output twice out of five. That is a statement about strings. It
tells a reader nothing about whether a re-run would change a reported RESULT. This
converts it into a result-level number: **a cold re-run changes mean CRPS by X.**

WHAT IT ACTUALLY RE-RUNS, stated precisely because the earlier description was
narrower than the implementation. The control builds its provider with
`cached=False`, so ALL THREE AGENTS run fresh -- not the analyst alone. Intake and
the structuralist are temperature 0 and near-deterministic; the analyst is
temperature 0.7. So the measurement is WHOLE-PIPELINE re-derivation variance, which
is what the README's claim is about, and it is a better instrument for that claim
than an analyst-only re-draw would have been.

WHAT IS REPORTED
  1. mean CRPS on the 60 items, cached versus cold, and the paired difference with
     a cluster-robust interval
  2. the per-item SD of that paired difference -- the quantity formerly called
     sigma_draw, now reported for its own sake rather than as a gate input
  3. the byte-identity rate of the cold forecasts against the stored ones, directly
     comparable to the existing 2-of-5 figure
  4. how many of the 60 items change their scenario numbers at all

DESCRIPTIVE ONLY. NO INFERENTIAL USE AND NO GATING ROLE. It tests no hypothesis,
enters no comparison, and corrects nothing. It is a variance measurement of a
system property the project already states publicly, and its only consumers are the
README's reproducibility table and the vault.

THERE IS NO TEST HERE TO BIAS, which is why re-purposing it after the fact is
legitimate where re-purposing a hypothesis test would not be. A gate has a decision
attached and can be moved to change an outcome; a variance measurement of a stated
property has no outcome to change. That distinction is the whole reason this record
exists rather than a silent reuse.

